      {
        "id": 63072,
        "name": "Ameena",
        "username": "Ameena",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-05-15T00:10:53.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Note that shuffling the trash back into the deck is true of <span class=\"bbcode-i\">all</span> decks - if you need to either draw, discard, or play from a deck but there aren't any cards left, you shuffle the trash to make a new deck but only when you actually need to draw or whatever - you don't reshuffle just because you've run out of cards, but leave the empty deck until you need to take a card from it. The only time you don't reshuffle when you run out of cards is when you <span class=\"bbcode-i\">reveal</span> cards. So in the example with the Operative, she needs to reveal cards until she gets an Underboss but none are left? Aaww, too bad for her ;). The same goes for when you need to reveal a specific number of cards, for example Arcane Cadence (in the Argent Adept's deck), which tells you to reveal the top five cards of your deck. If you have less than five cards remaining in your deck, you reveal as many as are left but lose out on the rest. So, best not play that card if you have less than five in your deck, unless you <span class=\"bbcode-i\">really need</span> to play one of those cards <span class=\"bbcode-i\">right now</span> ;).</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:39:51.146Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
