        "created_at": "2013-05-15T21:06:22.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ronway\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/48/1856_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ronway:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>That is true, but I always thought that even if it doesn't say \"then\" it would still be done in order. As you could manage to chain all 4 Arcane Cadance and end up with 4 sperate stacks of various sizes and not remember what you did with each of those decks already and cause a lot of chaos.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I'm with Ronway on this. You drew four cards instead of five? You get to do the first four things, not any four you want.</p>",
